@module render ; The renderer: the sprite composer, the cell drawers, the scroll and the attributes
@about Nothing is drawn on the screen but whole cells. The map builder $88D4 fills ViewCells $6B00 (32 x 44 cell numbers; row 8 is the screen's row 0, the HUD, so screen rows 1-23 are view rows 9-31), and DirtyMap $6600 (DirtyMap + $500 = ViewCells, same index) says what each screen cell needs: 0 nothing, 1 the level cell again, n >= 2 the composed spare cell n.
@about A sprite is masked into copies, never into the screen: ComposeSprite $7329 asks ComposeCell $7755 for each cell under the sprite, which copies the cell's 8 bytes (or the spare cell another sprite already made there) into the next spare cell (SpareCells + 8 x (n + 1), n = SpareCount $77B0), marks DirtyMap with n and leaves a cell whose CellFlags bit 7 is set alone (the sprite passes behind it). The spare cells of one sprite form a strip, column by column, 24 or 32 bytes a column, and the composer masks the sprite's rows into the strip ((byte AND mask) OR data, 3 bytes a row, 4 when the sprite is shifted), popping the rows with SP. DrawChangedCells $76D4 then copies the spare cells to the screen and restores the level cells the sprites left (1 -> 0, n -> 1), so a pass redraws only the cells sprites touch.
@about The view scrolls by 8 cell rows (ScrollDown $78A5, ScrollUp $7905) in three steps of 2, 4 and 2 rows, one frame each, redrawing only the cells that differ from what the screen shows (RedrawScrolledView $77B1); attributes are set per cell from CellAttrs (SetViewAttrs $783F for the whole view, the scroll per redrawn cell).

$7329 c ComposeSprite ; Mask the sprite of the object record at IX into spare copies of the cells under it
> IX = an object record: +1 x in pixels, +2/+3 y in pixels from the top of the view buffer (64 = the screen's top), +4/+5 the sprite's address (0: nothing drawn), +6 bit 7 mirrored. The sprite (in Sprites $C26D) is: a byte added to the strip offset (the sprite's top line), a byte of rows, then 6 bytes a row: data 2, data 1, data 0, mask 0, mask 2, mask 1 (popped as HL, BC, DE). Returns at once when y >= 299 ($012B: below the buffer) or the sprite address is 0.
> The view cell under the top left is ViewCells + (y AND $F8) x 4 + x / 8; the first spare cell SpareCells + 8 x (SpareCount + 1). x AND 7 = 0 (aligned): 3 columns, of 4 cells when y AND 4 (else 3), each through ComposeCell $7755, then the rows are masked in at IY = the strip + (y AND 7) + the sprite's first byte, columns w = 32 (or 24) bytes apart, the displacements patched into $7495-$74AC. Otherwise (shifted, ComposeShifted $74B7): 4 columns, each row shifted right by x AND 7 through the chain $7637 entered at $7637 + 14 x (x AND 7), a fourth byte of data (0) and mask ($FF) shifted in. A mirrored sprite swaps its outer bytes and reverses every byte through MirrorTable $6500 ($7471, $760B).
> Interrupts are off while SP walks the sprite ($7442-$74B5, $75DC-$76D2): an interrupt that falls there is lost. SP is put back from the copy stored at $74B3 / $76D0.
> Callers: the object drawer $85FA ($860A, $8618, $8626, $8639, $8652) and the menu's $814B. 250 504 runs in 65 builds; aligned 118 841 (3 rows 113 446, 4 rows 5395), shifted 108 333 (3 rows 96 247, 4 rows 13 402); mirrored rows 232 085 aligned, 551 698 shifted.
