@module interrupt
$7A76 b Machine48K ; $FF on a 48K (no RAM 1: no music, beeper effects), 0 on a 128K
> Set by the entry code $7B8F; read by CallRam1 $7A77, PlayEffect $7A97, the level start ($7CAD, $7CDB, $7CDE) and the main loop $7D80 (CALL NZ the beeper step). 0 in every recording (all 128K).

$7A77 c CallRam1 ; Call HL in RAM 1 with A, interrupts off; nothing on a 48K
> Stores A and HL into its own LD A,n and CALL nn, returns at once when Machine48K is set, else DI, port $7FFD = $11 (RAM 1 at $C000, ROM 1), the call, $7FFD = $10 (RAM 0). Interrupts stay off: the IM 2 handler's EI or the next WaitFrames puts them back. 133 677 runs in 68 builds: MusicFrameCall 127 035, PlayEffect 6585, StartTune 57.
