@module interrupt
$81AF c Random ; A pseudo-random byte from the tick count: A and RandomValue
> HL = RandomValue + Ticks (low word) + 13 + Ticks (high word) with the carry; A (as given) XOR L XOR D XOR E XOR H becomes L; HL stored in RandomValue; A is the result. HL and DE kept.
> Evidence: 1018 runs in 21 builds (callers $A010 x999, $A016 x995, $A048 x19, $A05F x18).
> Witness: L1 3010 (rzx-l1-00000-poke, rzx-l1-02000-poke, rzx-l1-04000-poke, rzx-l1-08000-poke, rzx-l1-16000-poke, rzx-l1-20000-poke, rzx-l1-24000-poke, rzx-l2-00000-poke, rzx-l2-20000-poke, rzx-l3-00000-poke, rzx-l3-02000-poke, rzx-l3-06000-poke, rzx-l4-02000-poke, rzx-l4-04000-poke, rzx-l4-16000-poke, rzx-l4-18000-poke, rzx-l5-04000-poke, rzx-l5-06000-poke, rzx-l5-12000-poke, c48, load-l2, load-l3, sec-l2-s7, sec-l2-s12, sec-l3-s5, sec-l4-s12, sec-l5-s5).

$81CE w RandomValue 1 ; The last random word (Random)

$81D0 w Ticks 2 ; The interrupts counted, 32 bits: the low word, then the high word
> Counted by CountTicks every interrupt, read by Random.

$81D4 c CountTicks ; Ticks + 1 (32 bits); called by the IM 2 handler
> The low word + 1; when it wraps to 0 the high word + 1.
> Evidence: 127 035 runs in 68 builds, every call from $FF0E (the handler at $FEFE: the copy of $7C49); c1 4706.
> Witness: L1 324903 (cheats, controls-cursor, controls-kempston, controls-keyboard, controls-sinclair, end-congrats, long-l4, rzx-l1-00000-poke, rzx-l1-02000-poke, rzx-l1-04000-poke, rzx-l1-06000-poke, rzx-l1-08000-poke, rzx-l1-10000-poke, rzx-l1-12000-poke, rzx-l1-14000-poke, rzx-l1-16000-poke, rzx-l1-18000-poke, rzx-l1-20000-poke, rzx-l1-22000-poke, rzx-l1-24000-poke, rzx-l2-00000-poke, rzx-l2-02000-poke, rzx-l2-04000-poke, rzx-l2-06000-poke, rzx-l2-08000-poke, rzx-l2-10000-poke, rzx-l2-12000-poke, rzx-l2-14000-poke, rzx-l2-16000-poke, rzx-l2-18000-poke, rzx-l2-20000-poke, rzx-l2-22000-poke, rzx-l2-24000-poke, rzx-l3-00000-poke, rzx-l3-02000-poke, rzx-l3-04000-poke, rzx-l3-06000-poke, rzx-l3-08000-poke, rzx-l3-10000-poke, rzx-l4-00000-poke, rzx-l4-02000-poke, rzx-l4-04000-poke, rzx-l4-06000-poke, rzx-l4-08000-poke, rzx-l4-10000-poke, rzx-l4-12000-poke, rzx-l4-14000-poke, rzx-l4-16000-poke, rzx-l4-18000-poke, rzx-l4-20000-poke, rzx-l5-00000-poke, rzx-l5-02000-poke, rzx-l5-04000-poke, rzx-l5-06000-poke, rzx-l5-08000-poke, rzx-l5-10000-poke, rzx-l5-12000-poke, rzx-l5-14000-poke, rzx-l5-16000-poke, rzx-l5-18000-poke, rzx-l5-20000-poke, rzx-l5-22000-poke, rzx-l5-23000, rzx-l5-24000-poke, rzx-l5-26000-poke, rzx-l5-full, sec-l1-s8, c1, c48, load-l2-load-l5, sec-l2-s7, sec-l2-s10-sec-l2-s12, sec-l3-s3-sec-l3-s5, sec-l3-s7-sec-l3-s9, sec-l4-s x5, sec-l5-s3, sec-l5-s5).

@module menu
$81E6 c MoveLetters ; Move every falling letter one frame and compose it into the view
> The composed cells from 2 ($77B0); for each 8-byte record from $7B8F until $FF: MoveLetter, ComposeLetter.
> Evidence: 4731 runs in 11 builds (from DropTextFrame).
> Witness: L1 25150 (controls-cursor, controls-kempston, controls-keyboard, controls-sinclair, end-congrats, rzx-l5-23000, rzx-l5-full, sec-l1-s8, c1, c48, load-l2-load-l5, sec-l2-s7, sec-l2-s10-sec-l2-s12, sec-l3-s3-sec-l3-s5, sec-l3-s7-sec-l3-s9, sec-l4-s x5, sec-l5-s3, sec-l5-s5).

$81EF c MoveLettersLoop ; The next letter record
> Ends at a record whose +0 is $FF; IX + 8.
> Evidence: the loop of MoveLetters (reads $7B8F-$7C4F).
> Witness: L1 330002 (controls-cursor, controls-kempston, controls-keyboard, controls-sinclair, end-congrats, rzx-l5-23000, rzx-l5-24000-poke, rzx-l5-full, sec-l1-s8, c1, c48, load-l2-load-l5, sec-l2-s7, sec-l2-s10-sec-l2-s12, sec-l3-s3-sec-l3-s5, sec-l3-s7-sec-l3-s9, sec-l4-s x5, sec-l5-s3, sec-l5-s5).

$8203 c MoveLetter ; One letter's fall: delay, gravity, a bounce at its row
> IX = the record (BuildLetters): +0 glyph, +1 column, +2/+3 y (+2 the pixel row, +3 the fraction), +4/+5 the speed (+4 low), +6 the delay in frames, +7 the row it stops at. While the delay is not 0 it counts down (the letters start one after the other, 6 frames apart). Then speed + $60 (the gravity), y + speed; past the row: y = the row, speed = - speed / 2 (a bounce), 0 when its high byte is 0 or $FF (the letter stops).
> Evidence: 57 671 runs in 12 builds.
> Witness: L1 304850 (controls-cursor, controls-kempston, controls-keyboard, controls-sinclair, end-congrats, rzx-l5-23000, rzx-l5-24000-poke, rzx-l5-full, sec-l1-s8, c1, c48, load-l2-load-l5, sec-l2-s7, sec-l2-s10-sec-l2-s12, sec-l3-s3-sec-l3-s5, sec-l3-s7-sec-l3-s9, sec-l4-s x5, sec-l5-s3, sec-l5-s5).
$820E LetterFall ; speed + gravity, y + speed
$8248 LetterStop ; too slow to bounce: speed 0
$824B LetterBounce ; the new speed
$8251 LetterStoreY ; y stored

$8258 c BuildLetters ; One falling-letter record per character of a text, from $7B8F
> HL = the text ($FF the end), D = the row it falls to (pixels), E = the column. Each non-space character: +0 the glyph (code - $34), +1 the column, +2/+3 y = $4000 (row 64), +4/+5 speed = $0900 (9 pixels a frame down), +6 the delay C (1, then 6 more for every character, spaces too), +7 the row D. The record after the last gets $FF at +0. Out: HL on the text's $FF.
> Evidence: 41 runs in 11 builds (writes $7B8F-$7C4F).
> Witness: L1 226 (controls-cursor, controls-kempston, controls-keyboard, controls-sinclair, end-congrats, rzx-l5-23000, rzx-l5-full, sec-l1-s8, c1, c48, load-l2-load-l5, sec-l2-s7, sec-l2-s10-sec-l2-s12, sec-l3-s3-sec-l3-s5, sec-l3-s7-sec-l3-s9, sec-l4-s x5, sec-l5-s3, sec-l5-s5).
$825E BuildLettersLoop ; the next character
$8299 BuildLettersNext ; column + 1, delay + 6

$82A1 c PutTextCells ; Put a text's glyph numbers into the view buffer, marked for redraw
> HL = the text, DE = the view buffer address ($6B00 + 32 x row + column). Each non-space character: the glyph number (code - $34) at DE and 1 at DE - $500 (the old buffer at $6600, so the drawer sees a change).
> Evidence: 97 runs in 12 builds (writes $67A7-$695D and $6CA7-$6E5D).
> Witness: L1 639 (controls-cursor, controls-kempston, controls-keyboard, controls-sinclair, end-congrats, rzx-l5-23000, rzx-l5-24000-poke, rzx-l5-full, sec-l1-s8, c1, c48, load-l2-load-l5, sec-l2-s7, sec-l2-s10-sec-l2-s12, sec-l3-s3-sec-l3-s5, sec-l3-s7-sec-l3-s9, sec-l4-s x5, sec-l5-s3, sec-l5-s5).
$82A3 PutTextCellsLoop ; the next character
$82B8 PutTextCellsNext ; the next column

$82BD c DropText ; Show a text in the view: A = $FF letters fall into place, else at once
> HL = the text, D = the row in pixels, E = the column, A = $FF to animate. Stores the text and its view buffer address ($6B00 + 4 x (D AND $F8) + E) into DropTextFinish's operands. A = $FF: BuildLetters, then DropTextWait's frames until every letter has stopped or a number key is pressed. Then (and at once when A is not $FF) DropTextFinish puts the text into the view buffer and redraws it. Out: A = the key pressed during the fall (ReadMenuKey: 0-5), $FF when none, or A as given when not animated; HL on the text's $FF (the end pointer of the last animated text). The callers chain A: after a key the later texts of the menu are put at once, and the key is the menu's choice.
> Evidence: 97 runs in 11 builds (callers: LevelMenu, ControlMenu, GameOver $7E8B, ShowEndTextLoop $8777).
> Witness: L1 639 (controls-cursor, controls-kempston, controls-keyboard, controls-sinclair, end-congrats, rzx-l5-23000, rzx-l5-full, sec-l1-s8, c1, c48, load-l2-load-l5, sec-l2-s7, sec-l2-s10-sec-l2-s12, sec-l3-s3-sec-l3-s5, sec-l3-s7-sec-l3-s9, sec-l4-s x5, sec-l5-s3, sec-l5-s5).
$82DF DropTextFrame ; one frame of the fall

$82E2 c DropTextWait ; Wait a frame, redraw, stop at a key or when every letter has stopped
> Frame wait (C = 1), the cells redrawn ($76D4), ReadMenuKey: a key goes to DropTextFinish with A = the key. Else, a letter with a delay or a speed left (+6 or +5 not 0) means another frame (DropTextFrame); all still: DropTextFinish.
> Evidence: 4732 runs in 12 builds.
> Witness: L1 25152 (controls-cursor, controls-kempston, controls-keyboard, controls-sinclair, end-congrats, rzx-l5-23000, rzx-l5-24000-poke, rzx-l5-full, sec-l1-s8, c1, c48, load-l2-load-l5, sec-l2-s7, sec-l2-s10-sec-l2-s12, sec-l3-s3-sec-l3-s5, sec-l3-s7-sec-l3-s9, sec-l4-s x5, sec-l5-s3, sec-l5-s5).
$82F9 DropTextCheckLoop ; is any letter still moving?
$830F DropTextFinish ; the text put in the view buffer (self-modified operands: the text, the buffer address, HL out)

$8321 c ComposeLetter ; Compose a falling letter into spare cells of the view
> The next spare cell is $5DF0 + 8 x $77B0 (the composed cells $5DE8 + 8n). The view cell under the letter (row (y AND $F8) / 8, its column) and, when y is not on a cell boundary, the one below are copied into spare cells by $7755 (which puts the spare cells' numbers into the view buffer). Then the glyph $7080 + 8 x (+0) is ORed in from the row y AND 7 of the first spare cell on (eight rows over the two cells).
> Evidence: 57 671 runs in 12 builds (reads the glyphs $7080-$71AF, writes $5E00-$5F0E).
> Witness: L1 304850 (controls-cursor, controls-kempston, controls-keyboard, controls-sinclair, end-congrats, rzx-l5-23000, rzx-l5-24000-poke, rzx-l5-full, sec-l1-s8, c1, c48, load-l2-load-l5, sec-l2-s7, sec-l2-s10-sec-l2-s12, sec-l3-s3-sec-l3-s5, sec-l3-s7-sec-l3-s9, sec-l4-s x5, sec-l5-s3, sec-l5-s5).
$8352 ComposeLetterRows ; the glyph ORed in at the letter's row
$836C ComposeLetterLoop ; one of the eight rows

@module level ; The sections' objects reset at a new game
@about A section's record in the section table ($C202, 8 bytes) holds at +6/+7 the offset of its objects list: 4-byte records, +0 the kind (bit 7 set once the object is used), +3 bits 0-1 the number of 4-byte extensions. ResetSectionObjects clears bit 7 in every record of the level's sections at a new game.

$8374 b SectionCounts 5 ; The number of sections of each level: 9, 13, 10, 13, 8
> Read by ResetSectionObjects at SectionCounts - 1 + Level.
@res tables/section-counts.bin

$8379 c ResetSectionObjects ; Clear bit 7 (used) in every object record of every section of the level
> B = SectionCounts[Level]; for each section's 8-byte record from ($C202) + 6: the list at ($C202) + the big-endian word at +6; each 4-byte record until a kind 0: its byte +0 AND $7F, then skip as many more 4-byte records as +3 AND 3 says.
> Evidence: 12 runs in 11 builds (level 1: reads $ECF3-$ED2C and the lists $ED32-$F1FE, writes $ED32-$F1EC).
> Witness: L1 56 (controls-cursor, controls-kempston, controls-keyboard, controls-sinclair, rzx-l1-00000-poke, rzx-l5-full, sec-l1-s8, c1, c48, load-l2-load-l5, sec-l2-s7, sec-l2-s10-sec-l2-s12, sec-l3-s3-sec-l3-s5, sec-l3-s7-sec-l3-s9, sec-l4-s x5, sec-l5-s3, sec-l5-s5).
$838B ResetSectionLoop ; a section
$8397 ResetRecordLoop ; an object record
$83A9 SkipExtraLoop ; its extensions
$83AF ResetSectionNext ; the next section's record

@module objects ; The two object tables over the entry code
@about Table A: six 24-byte records from $7B8F (update $A2F7, end mark $7C1F); table B: four 23-byte records from $7C20 (update $9EAF, end mark $7C7C). A record with +0 = 0 is free. Both are cleared at every new game, as are the entry code's bytes they lie on.

$83B8 c ClearObjectTables ; Clear $7B8F-$7C7C and put the end marks of the two tables
> $7B8F-$7C7C = 0 (238 bytes), $FF at $7C1F (the end of table A) and at $7C7C (the end of table B).
> Evidence: 12 runs in 11 builds, from StartGame.
> Witness: L1 56 (controls-cursor, controls-kempston, controls-keyboard, controls-sinclair, rzx-l1-00000-poke, rzx-l5-full, sec-l1-s8, c1, c48, load-l2-load-l5, sec-l2-s7, sec-l2-s10-sec-l2-s12, sec-l3-s3-sec-l3-s5, sec-l3-s7-sec-l3-s9, sec-l4-s x5, sec-l5-s3, sec-l5-s5).

@module menu
$83CE c MoveMenuRick ; The control menu's Rick: y toward the row C, x swinging about 24
> y ($9BAD) moves 2 toward C. The x speed $9B95 (a word) gets + $30 while x ($9BAC) is below $18, - $30 when it is at or above; x and its fraction ($9B97) + speed: Rick sways sideways.
> Evidence: 2219 runs in 10 builds (from ControlMenuPointer).
> Witness: L1 8338 (controls-cursor, controls-kempston, controls-keyboard, controls-sinclair, rzx-l5-full, sec-l1-s8, c1, c48, load-l2-load-l5, sec-l2-s7, sec-l2-s10-sec-l2-s12, sec-l3-s3-sec-l3-s5, sec-l3-s7-sec-l3-s9, sec-l4-s x5, sec-l5-s3, sec-l5-s5).
$83E1 MenuRickMoveY ; y + the step
$83F9 MenuRickMoveX ; x + speed

@module levelload ; The tape level loader
@about A level not in memory is read from side B: LoadLevel prints "START TAPE ON SIDE TWO", reads the next block into $A800 (21 760 bytes) and goes on until the block read is the wanted level (its LevelNumber, $C20C), then prints "STOP TAPE AND PRESS FIRE" and waits for fire. The loader is the ROM's LD-BYTES with the bits shifted in from the top (LD L,$80 / RR L), the verify branch removed and the parity test LD A,H / CPL / CP 1: side B's bytes are stored bit-reversed (stage 1). The RZX run's version has another loader here ($846A-$8510, a TAP version).

$840C c LoadLevel ; Read side B until the wanted level is in, then wait for fire
> $7A61, "START TAPE ON SIDE TWO" at $4845 (PrintText), LoadLevelBlock; LevelNumber not equal to Level: again (the blocks before the wanted one are read and dropped). Then $7A61, "STOP TAPE AND PRESS FIRE" at $4843 and LoadLevelWaitFire.
> Evidence: 16 runs in 6 builds (load-l2 2, load-l3 3, load-l4 4, load-l5 5: one more than the level's block number, side B holding levels 1-5 in order; rzx-l3-10000-poke 1, rzx-l4-20000-poke 1 run the RZX run's version).
> Witness: L1 18 (rzx-l3-10000-poke, rzx-l4-20000-poke, load-l2-load-l5).
$841E ; NOP (a byte the TAP version patches?)
$842A ; "STOP TAPE AND PRESS FIRE"

$8433 c LoadLevelWaitFire ; Wait for fire, SPACE or ENTER after the load
> $7229 until Z.
> Evidence: 1 078 823 runs in 9 builds.
> Witness: L1 1238557 (rzx-l2-00000-poke, rzx-l3-00000-poke, rzx-l4-00000-poke, rzx-l5-00000-poke, rzx-l5-full, load-l2-load-l5, sec-l2-s7, sec-l2-s10-sec-l2-s12, sec-l3-s3-sec-l3-s5, sec-l3-s7-sec-l3-s9, sec-l4-s x5, sec-l5-s3, sec-l5-s5).

$843A t TapeTexts ; "START TAPE ON SIDE TWO", "STOP TAPE AND PRESS FIRE"
> Printed by LoadLevel with PrintText; $FF ends each.
@res texts/tape.bin
$8451 StopTapeText ; "STOP TAPE AND PRESS FIRE"

$846A c LoadLevelBlock ; Load one bit-reversed block of 21 760 bytes into $A800
> IX = $A800, DE = 21 760, A = $FF (the flag of a data block), carry set (load): LdBytes, then EI (the loader leaves interrupts off).
> Evidence: 16 runs in 6 builds.
> Witness: L1 18 (rzx-l3-10000-poke, rzx-l4-20000-poke, load-l2-load-l5).

$8479 c LdBytes ; LD-BYTES with the bits reversed: IX the address, DE the length, A the flag
> The ROM's $0556 step for step: DI, border 7 ($0F), LdBytesEnd pushed as the return, the leader, the sync, the flag byte, then the bytes. The differences from the ROM: each byte is shifted in from the top (L = $80, RR L), so the tape's bytes are stored bit-reversed; the verify branch is gone (every byte is stored); the end test is LD A,H / CPL / CP 1: carry when the XOR of the block was $FF. SPACE breaks (carry clear).
> Evidence: 14 runs in 4 builds (load-l2 ... load-l5; writes $A800-$FCFF; port $FE in and out).
> Witness: L1 14 (load-l2-load-l5).
$848E LdBreak ; RET NZ: a break
$848F LdStart ; wait for the first edge
$8497 LdWait ; a pause of about a second
$84A3 LdLeader ; the leader tone
$84B2 LdSync ; the sync pulses
$84CC LdLoop ; a byte: the flag byte first
$84D1 LdStore ; the byte stored (the ROM's verify is gone)
$84D6 LdFlag ; the flag byte compared
$84E0 LdNext ; IX + 1
$84E2 LdDec ; DE - 1
$84E6 LdMarker ; L = $80: the byte comes in from the top
$84E8 LdEightBits ; a bit: RR L (the ROM: RL L)
$84FD ; the checksum: CPL / CP 1, the XOR must be $FF

$8502 c LdEdge2 ; Two edges (the ROM's LD-EDGE-2)
> LdEdge1 twice.
> Evidence: 2 440 942 runs in 4 builds.
> Witness: L1 2440942 (load-l2-load-l5).

$8506 c LdEdge1 ; One edge (the ROM's LD-EDGE-1): B counts the time, the border flashes
> A delay of $16 loops, then B + 1 per sample of port $FE until the EAR bit changes; carry set on an edge (the border colour changed: (C AND 7) OR 8), clear on a time out (B wraps) or SPACE.
> Evidence: 4 899 114 runs in 4 builds (port $7FFE in, $FE out).
> Witness: L1 4899114 (load-l2-load-l5).
$8508 LdEdgeDelay ; the delay before the samples
$850C LdSample ; a sample of the EAR bit

$8524 c LdBytesEnd ; The loader's return: black border, or the load error
> Carry (a good block): border 0, return to LoadLevelBlock. No carry: LoadError.
> Evidence: 14 runs in 4 builds, every load good.
> Witness: L1 14 (load-l2-load-l5).

$852A c LoadError ; POP HL / JP $8452: a load error
@isub $852B JP StopTapeText+1
@over $8452 ; the JP lands inside the text "STOP TAPE AND PRESS FIRE": text, never run (no load error in any recording)
> The code bytes POP HL (the return to LoadLevelBlock dropped) and JP $8452, an address inside "STOP TAPE AND PRESS FIRE" ($8451): it would run the text as code. Probably an address from an earlier layout. Not executed in any recording (no load failed); a bad block would run it.
> Witness: L1 0 ().

$852E b LoaderFill 16 ; 204 bytes of $C9 (RET) up to $85F9
> Not read or run by any recording.

