@module ending ; The bonus tally, the two end texts
@about The Fat Guy's end (LevelsDone = 5): BonusTally adds 100 000, then 5000 for each bullet and 10 000 for each detonator left, TallyLives 100 000 for each life, each with an effect and a pause, and ShowEndText shows "AND SO RICK SAVES THE DAY ...". The other end (level 4 done without level 5 open, or level 5 done in a game that did not start at level 1): Congratulations shows "CONGRATULATIONS YOU HAVE COMPLETED LEVEL n HOWEVER ...". Both wait 2500 frames or fire, then go through GAME OVER to the control menu.

$86E0 c BonusTally ; The Fat Guy's end: 100 000, then the bullets and detonators counted
> The code bytes: LD HL,$7F11 / CALL $7ED3 (Points100000); then while ammunition ($8B3C) is not 0: one off, Points5000 ($7F05), effect 4 ($7A97), the HUD's ammunition ($79D1), 10 frames ($7A53); then while detonators ($8B3D) are not 0: one off, Points10000 ($7F0B), the HUD's detonators ($79DF), effect 5, 15 frames; then TallyLives. Jumped to from MainLoopPause ($7DB3). Not executed in the L1 builds: the RZX run went through it before frame 23 000, and rzx-l5-23000 starts in TallyLives.
> Witness: L1 0 ().
$86E0 ; LD HL,$7F11 / CALL $7ED3: 100 000
$86E6 TallyBullets ; the bullets: LD A,($8B3C) / AND A / JP Z,$8707
$86ED ; DEC A / LD ($8B3C),A / LD HL,$7F05 / CALL $7ED3: 5000
$86F7 ; LD A,4 / CALL $7A97 / CALL $79D1 / LD C,10 / CALL $7A53 / JP $86E6
$8707 TallyDetonators ; the detonators: LD A,($8B3D) / AND A / JP Z,$8728
$870E ; DEC A / LD ($8B3D),A / LD HL,$7F0B / CALL $7ED3: 10 000
$8718 ; CALL $79DF / LD A,5 / CALL $7A97 / LD C,15 / CALL $7A53 / JP $8707

$8728 c TallyLives ; Each life left: 100 000 points, an effect, 20 frames; then the Fat Guy's end text
> While lives ($8B3B) are not 0: one off, Points100000 (AddScore), the HUD's lives ($79C3), effect 10 ($7A97), 20 frames. Then tune 10 ($7AAD) and ShowEndText with FatGuyEndText.
> Evidence: rzx-l5-23000 6 runs (5 lives counted, the 6th pass to TallyDone), the ending text on its screens (stage 1: the RZX run's level 5, frames 23 200-26 500).
> Witness: L1 12 (rzx-l5-23000).
$8749 TallyDone ; tune 10, the Fat Guy's end text

$8754 c Congratulations ; The other end: the level's digit into the text, tune 0
> The code bytes LD A,($7EF1) / ADD A,$34 / LD ($87CD),A (the level as a text digit, stored 4 higher) / XOR A / CALL $7AAD (tune 0) / LD HL,$87A0 (CongratulationsText), falling into ShowEndText. Jumped to from MainLoopPause at $7DBB (level 5 done before five levels in this game) and $7DC7 (level 4 done with level 5 closed). Not executed in any recording: complete level 4 in a game that has not opened level 5 (from level 2, 3 or 4) to run it.
> Evidence: end-congrats (stage 2: the RZX run's level 4 end with POKE LevelsDone ($7EF2) = 0, so Level5Open stays clear) once: "CONGRATULATIONS ... YOU HAVE COMPLETED LEVEL 4" on its screens.
> Witness: L1 2 (end-congrats).
$8754 ; the level's digit into the text
$875C ; tune 0
$875F ; LD HL,$87A0: the text

$8763 c ShowEndText ; An end text: the view cleared, then each line falls into place
> HL = the list (CongratulationsText or FatGuyEndText). FontCellsMode, $796F (HL kept), then ShowEndTextLoop.
> Evidence: rzx-l5-23000 once.
> Witness: L1 4 (end-congrats, rzx-l5-23000).

$876B c ShowEndTextLoop ; A line of the end text: column, row, text
> A record: +0 the column (E), +1 the row in pixels (D), the text to $FF; DropText with A = $FF. A record starting with $FF ends the list: EndTextPause.
> Evidence: 6 runs in 2 builds (rzx-l5-23000 5, rzx-l5-24000-poke 1).
> Witness: L1 26 (end-congrats, rzx-l5-23000, rzx-l5-24000-poke).

$877A c ShowEndTextNext ; Past the line's $FF to the next record
> HL + 1, then ShowEndTextLoop.
> Evidence: rzx-l5-23000 (the four lines).
> Witness: L1 22 (end-congrats, rzx-l5-23000, rzx-l5-24000-poke).

$877E c EndTextPause ; 2500 frames or fire
> BC = 2500, then EndTextWait.
> Evidence: 2 runs in 2 builds (rzx-l5-23000, rzx-l5-24000-poke).
> Witness: L1 6 (end-congrats, rzx-l5-23000, rzx-l5-24000-poke).

$8781 c EndTextWait ; A frame; fire, SPACE or ENTER ends the wait
> Frame wait (C = 1), $7229; a key or BC = 0: EndTextExit.
> Evidence: 4512 runs in 3 builds (rzx-l5-23000 2256, rzx-l5-24000-poke 2000, rzx-l5-26000-poke 256): no recording reaches the end of the wait or a key.
> Witness: L1 11612 (end-congrats, rzx-l5-23000, rzx-l5-24000-poke, rzx-l5-26000-poke).

$8794 c EndTextExit ; After an end text: GAME OVER and the control menu
> The code bytes CALL $88B1 (FontCellsMode) / CALL $7EB3 (LevelCellsMode) / CALL $796F / JP $7E1E (GameOver: the "GAME  OVER" box, then the control menu). Not executed in any recording (rzx-l5-26000-poke ends inside EndTextWait).
> Witness: L1 0 ().

$87A0 t CongratulationsText ; The other end's text: records of column, row, text
> Records: +0 the column, +1 the row in pixels, the text, $FF; a $FF record ends the list. The digit at $87CD is written by Congratulations (Level + $34). Shown by ShowEndText.
@res texts/end-congratulations.bin
$87B2 ; "YOU HAVE COMPLETED LEVEL 9": the digit patched
$87CD CompletedLevelDigit ; the level, + $34
$87CF ; "HOWEVER TO COMPLETE THE GAME"
$87EE ; "PROPERLY YOU MUST COMPLETE ALL"
$880F ; "LEVELS IN ONE GAME STARTING"
$882D ; "FROM LEVEL 5": 1, the digit stored 4 higher
$883C ; the end of the list

$883D t FatGuyEndText ; The Fat Guy's end text: records of column, row, text
> "AND SO RICK SAVES THE DAY / BY DEFEATING THE FAT GUY AND / HIS FLEET OF ROBOT STARSHIPS / WHAT WILL RICK DO NEXT", in the same records as CongratulationsText. Shown by TallyLives through ShowEndText (rzx-l5-23000).
@res texts/end-fat-guy.bin
$8859 ; "BY DEFEATING THE FAT GUY AND"
$8878 ; "HIS FLEET OF ROBOT STARSHIPS"
$8897 ; "WHAT WILL RICK DO NEXT"
$88B0 ; the end of the list

@module render
$88B1 c FontCellsMode ; The cell drawer on the font; screen and buffers cleared
> Writes $7080 (the font) to the drawer's bases $7730 and $7777 and three zeros (NOPs) over the JP M at $775A, then $7A61, $8985, $8977. HL kept.
> Evidence: 16 runs in 11 builds (callers LevelMenu, ControlMenu, ShowEndText).
> Witness: L1 100 (controls-cursor, controls-kempston, controls-keyboard, controls-sinclair, end-congrats, rzx-l5-23000, rzx-l5-full, sec-l1-s8, c1, c48, load-l2-load-l5, sec-l2-s7, sec-l2-s10-sec-l2-s12, sec-l3-s3-sec-l3-s5, sec-l3-s7-sec-l3-s9, sec-l4-s x5, sec-l5-s3, sec-l5-s5).

@module level
$88CF b ViewTopRow ; The view's top row in the section (cells)
> Set by the section setup $8A6D (from LevelStarts +1 or the section entered) and by $8A26; moved by the scrolls $7905 (up) and $78A5 (down); read by the map builder $88D4, MainLoopPause's scroll tests, $8993 and others.

$88D0 w ViewMap 1 ; The section's map: the maps' base + the section's offset
> Set by $8A6D and $8A26, read by the map builder $88D4.

$88D2 b ViewLastRow ; The last top row the view may scroll down to in the section
> The section record's +3, set by $8A6D and $8A26; MainLoopPause scrolls down only while ViewTopRow is below it.

$88D3 b ExitDirection ; The exit Rick asks for in this pass: 0 none
> Cleared at each pass (MainLoopPause), set by Rick's movement ($945E, $95ED, $96B4, $988F, $9941) and by $8A26; when set, MainLoopPause runs the exit test $8993, which compares it with the exits' kinds (AND $0B).

@isub $8905 LD BC,Blocks
@isub $8914 LD BC,32-3
@isub $8935 LD BC,-3*32+1
@isub $893D LD BC,3*32
@isub $8D4F LD D,CellFlags/256
@isub $8E55 LD D,CellFlags/256
@isub $8E64 LD D,CellFlags/256
@isub $8E6F LD D,CellFlags/256
@isub $8E83 LD D,CellFlags/256

@module level ; Sections: the view built from the map, the exits, the section setup and the restart after a death
@about A level is a set of sections, each a shaft one screen wide whose map is a column of rows of 8 block numbers (a block is 4 x 4 cells). LevelHeader+2 points to the section table, 8 bytes a section: +0/+1 the map's offset from the maps' base (LevelHeader+4), big-endian; +2 not read by any code (0 in every level); +3 the last view top row the scroll may reach (cells); +4/+5 the offset of the section's exit list from the table's start, big-endian; +6/+7 the offset of its map entry list (enemies, traps, pickups: the objects module), big-endian. SetupSection reads it.
@about An exit list holds 4-byte records ended by a record whose bits 0, 1 and 3 are 0 (a 0 byte): +0 the flags (bits 0-1 the side: 1 left, 2 right; bit 4 keeps a bit-7 exit a level end under the long-levels switch $8067; bit 5 sets $945D to $FF on the way in; bit 6 sets LevelHookOn; bit 7 the level ends here), +1 the section row of Rick's feet at which the exit is taken, +2 the section entered, +3 the row of that section Rick's feet arrive at. CheckSectionExit takes an exit when Rick leaves the view at a side (the exit request $88D3 = 1 or 2). The view: ViewTop $88CF is the section row at the top of ViewCells; the scroll ($78A5, $7905) moves it by 8 rows and BuildView builds the 44 rows again.

$88D4 c BuildView ; Build ViewCells: 11 rows of 8 blocks from the section's map, from the view's top row
> The map row is ViewTop $88CF / 4, rounded down to an even row ((ViewTop x 2) AND $FFF0, ViewTop being a multiple of 8): the bytes from the section's map $88D0 plus that offset. Each map byte is a block number; the block's 16 cell numbers (Blocks + 16 x n, four rows of four) go to ViewCells as a 4 x 4 square, 8 blocks a row, 11 rows: 32 x 44 cells, $6B00-$707F.
> Runs with the interrupts off and SP borrowed: SP points at the block and POP DE takes two cell numbers at a time; the caller's SP is stored into the LD SP,n at $8946 and put back there (an interrupt in between is lost, NOTES). Then FindFirstMapEntry sets the map entry scan's start for the new view.
> Callers: the scroll down $78F2 (83 runs), the scroll up $7952 (89), SetupSection $8AE6 (97). Witness: 269 runs in 62 builds; reads the maps only ($E1ED-$E9D4 over all recordings), writes $6B00-$707F.
> Witness: L1 643 (controls-cursor, controls-kempston, controls-keyboard, controls-sinclair, long-l4, rzx-l1-00000-poke, rzx-l1-02000-poke, rzx-l1-04000-poke, rzx-l1-06000-poke, rzx-l1-08000-poke, rzx-l1-10000-poke, rzx-l1-12000-poke, rzx-l1-14000-poke, rzx-l1-16000-poke, rzx-l1-18000-poke, rzx-l1-20000-poke, rzx-l1-22000-poke, rzx-l1-24000-poke, rzx-l2-00000-poke, rzx-l2-02000-poke, rzx-l2-04000-poke, rzx-l2-06000-poke, rzx-l2-08000-poke, rzx-l2-10000-poke, rzx-l2-12000-poke, rzx-l2-14000-poke, rzx-l2-16000-poke, rzx-l2-18000-poke, rzx-l2-20000-poke, rzx-l2-22000-poke, rzx-l3-00000-poke, rzx-l3-02000-poke, rzx-l3-04000-poke, rzx-l3-06000-poke, rzx-l3-08000-poke, rzx-l3-10000-poke, rzx-l4-00000-poke, rzx-l4-02000-poke, rzx-l4-04000-poke, rzx-l4-06000-poke, rzx-l4-08000-poke, rzx-l4-10000-poke, rzx-l4-12000-poke, rzx-l4-14000-poke, rzx-l4-16000-poke, rzx-l4-18000-poke, rzx-l5-00000-poke, rzx-l5-02000-poke, rzx-l5-04000-poke, rzx-l5-06000-poke, rzx-l5-08000-poke, rzx-l5-10000-poke, rzx-l5-12000-poke, rzx-l5-14000-poke, rzx-l5-16000-poke, rzx-l5-18000-poke, rzx-l5-20000-poke, rzx-l5-full, sec-l1-s8, c1, c48, load-l2-load-l5, sec-l2-s7, sec-l2-s10-sec-l2-s12, sec-l3-s3-sec-l3-s5, sec-l3-s7-sec-l3-s9, sec-l4-s x5, sec-l5-s3, sec-l5-s5).
$88EF BuildViewDest ; HL' = the destination: the operand is set to ViewCells by $88EA
$88F4 ; the caller's SP into the LD SP,n at $8946
$88F8 BuildViewRow ; a row of 8 blocks
$88FA BuildViewBlock ; HL: the map byte; HL': the block's top left cell in ViewCells
$8909 ; SP = the block's 16 cell numbers
$8914 ; on to the next cell row, 3 columns back
$8935 ; back up 3 rows, on to the next block's column
