@module levelload ; The level's arrival: the maps' decipher
@about The level blocks on side B carry the last 768 bytes of each level's maps enciphered; DecryptMaps restores them once the level is in memory. Side A's resident level 1 is stored plain.

$894E c DecryptMaps ; Decipher the last 768 bytes of the level's maps
> The 768 bytes from the maps' base (LevelHeader+4) + $600: each byte XOR a key that starts at 0 and becomes (key XOR the byte's address low byte) + 1 after each byte. Run once per loaded level, by the level start $7CDB after the tape load $840C (not for level 1 from side A, which is stored plain).
> Evidence: 9 runs in 9 builds (load-l2 ... load-l5 and the RZX level starts 2-5, rzx-l5-full), each over $E7ED-$ED6C for levels with the base $E1ED (level 4) and the same 768 bytes above each base; the deciphered bytes equal the RZX run's memory (NOTES).
> Witness: L1 48 (rzx-l2-00000-poke, rzx-l3-00000-poke, rzx-l4-00000-poke, rzx-l5-00000-poke, rzx-l5-full, load-l2-load-l5, sec-l2-s7, sec-l2-s10-sec-l2-s12, sec-l3-s3-sec-l3-s5, sec-l3-s7-sec-l3-s9, sec-l4-s x5, sec-l5-s3, sec-l5-s5).
$895A DecryptMapsLoop

