@module collision ; Hit tests: points and boxes against boxes, the bullet's wall probe, the bomb's ground probe
@about The tests return C for a hit. A box is given as E (x), HL (y, pixels from the view's top, 16 bits), C (width) and B (height); a record at IX gives its own box as +1 (x), +2/+3 (y), +7 (width), +8 (height). Rick's box is x $9BAC + 4, y $9BAD (5 lower when he crawls, $9B98), 16 x 21 pixels (16 x 16 crawling).
@about The far cases (the two y differing by 256 or more) end in XOR A / RET or SCF / RET pairs that no recording ran and that the walk keeps as bytes (the read builds mark them read).

