@module weapons ; The gun and its bullet, the detonator and its blast, the punch
@about Rick's weapons are three records beside his own: the bullet BulletRecord ($9BB4) and the detonator DetonatorRecord ($9BBD), 9 bytes each like RickRecord (+0 active, +1 x, +2/+3 y, +4/+5 the sprite, +6 the mirror bit), and the punch, which has no record: PunchX / PunchY and the 10-pass PunchTimer, read by the enemy test $8C6C. The keys with fire held (UpdateRick, RickFireActions): up shoots (FireBullet, one bullet at a time, released between shots), down drops a detonator (DropDetonator, one at a time), left or right punches.
@about The detonator is thrown with Rick's sideways keys (-2, 0 or +2 pixels a pass), falls under gravity, slides with friction, lands on platforms and blocks, and burns 64 passes: 54 of physics, then 10 of blast (BurnFuse). During the blast passes 4-9 a 32 x 21 box round it kills Rick; a deadly cell sets it off at once.

$91B0 c MoveBullet ; Move the bullet 8 pixels a pass; it ends on a solid cell or the view's edge
> IX = BulletRecord (the object step $86B7, while BulletRecord +0 is set). Reads the cell flags at (x+4, y+4) through $8D0C: bit 1 (solid) ends the bullet (+0 = 0). Else x += BulletDx (+8 or -8): going left, x below 0 ends it; going right, a carry or x >= $F8 ends it. Hitting enemies and traps is tested elsewhere ($8BF3, $A528, $A69F read BulletRecord).
> Ran 755 times in 43 builds (c1 62, each control recording 1).
