@module objects ; The section's objects: spawning from the map, freeing, the trigger boxes, the scroll shift
@about A section's map carries a list of 4-byte entries, each followed by 0-3 trigger boxes of 4 bytes (scanned by $8B75): +0 the kind (bit 7 set while the object lives), +1 the cell row in the section, +2 the column (bits 0-4) with bit 5 = 4 pixels right and bit 6 = 3 pixels down, +3 the parameters (bits 0-1 the number of boxes, bits 2-5 the behaviour or the patrol length, bit 6 one-shot). A box is +0 the x in pixels, +1 the cell row, +2 the size (high nibble rows - 1, low nibble columns - 1), +3 who sets it off (bit 0 Rick, 1 the bullet, 2 the detonator's blast, 3 the punch box, 4 an enemy, 5 a trap; bit 6 fires on every pass, bit 7 the latch of a box that fired and is still occupied).
@about A map entry whose kind is below $74 becomes a trap or a pickup in the 24-byte records at $7B8F (SpawnMapObject, UpdateTrap); $78 and $7C start and stop the countdown bonus; any other kind from $74 up becomes an enemy in the 23-byte records at $7C20 (UpdateEnemy). Both lists end with a $FF byte; a record whose +0 is 0 is free. The y of every record is in pixels from the top of the view (16 bits), so the scroll ($78A5, $7905) shifts them all through ShiftObjects.

$9C57 c FreeObject ; Free the object record at IX and re-arm its map entry
> Clears bit 7 of the map entry the record points to (+$0C/+$0D; none when the word is 0) so the entry can spawn again, and clears +0, which frees the record. Called for every record when a section is set up ($9BEB), and when an object leaves the view (ShiftObjects, EnemyVertical, UpdateTrap).
> Input IX: an enemy or trap record. Witness: 476 runs in 56 builds (callers $9BFE 239, $9C19 206, $9E54 124, $9E7F 100, $A1CC 13, $A38E 44, $A39C 39, $A3CA 69).
