$9CAC StartBonusTimer ; kind $78: only when no countdown runs ($9BA9 = 0)
$9CB1 ; $9BA9 = $FF: the countdown runs ($865D calls $9163 each pass)
$9CB5 ; $9BAA = 25: passes per step of $9163 (10 points off every 25 passes)
$9CBA ; the bonus digits $7F17-$7F1C = 002000
$9CC4 ; tune 1
$9CCA StopBonusTimer ; kind $7C: only while the countdown runs
$9CD3 ; the digits left at $7F17 go to the score
$9CD9 ; tune 1 again
$9CDF SpawnEnemy ; a free 23-byte record at $7C20 ($9BD9), else return
$9CE7 ; +6 = 2: walking right (+6 is the x step, its bit 7 the mirror)
$9D00 ; +0 = the kind without bit 7; bits 0-1 the behaviour, bit 2 the sprite set
$9D05 ; the map entry marked alive
$9D0C ; x = column x 8
$9D17 ; y = (row - the view's top row $88CF) x 8 + 3
$9D2E ; +$0C/+$0D: the map entry
$9D37 ; both branches load the same script (+$0A/+$0B), which no enemy code reads
$9D44 SpawnEnemySetAnim
$9D4A ; +$13 = (bits 2-5 of the entry's +3, plus 1) x 8: the patrol length in pixels

$9D59 b EnemyAnimScripts 9 ; Three animation scripts the enemy spawn stores and nothing reads
> Frame numbers for SpriteFrameMap, each script closed by $FF and the address to loop to (the form AnimateTrap reads): frames $2A, $2A, $2B, $2B, $2C, $2C; $2D, $2E; $2F, $30. SpawnEnemy writes $9D59 into every enemy's +$0A/+$0B, but the enemies' sprites come from EnemyWalkSprites ($9ECE): no recording reads these bytes (l1q: the loader's writes only).
$9D62 EnemyAnimScript2 ; frames $2D, $2E, loop
$9D67 EnemyAnimScript3 ; frames $2F, $30, loop

$9D6C c SpawnMapObject ; Spawn a trap or pickup from a map entry (kind below $74)
> Takes a free 24-byte record at $7B8F ($9BC7; none: return) and fills it from the level's kind table, the word at LevelHeader (11 bytes a kind, addressed by kind x 2 through the table of pointers there): +7 width, +8 height, +2 bits 6-7 into +0 and bits 0-5 x 4 (with the new kind's bits 0-5) into +$15 (the kind to switch to), +3/+4 the path (+$0F/+$10), +5/+6 the animation (+$0A/+$0B), +7/+8 the second path (+$11/+$12), +9/+10 the second animation (+$13/+$14).
> +0 = 1 OR bits 2-5 of the entry's +3 OR the kind table's bits 6-7: bit 0 alive, bit 1 path paused, bits 2-4 the trigger behaviour (UpdateTrap $A4AA), bit 5 with bit 2 the pickup kinds ($21, $29, $2D), bit 6 deadly to Rick and enemies, bit 7 the detonator test. Behaviour $10 starts with +6 = $60 (bit 6: no trigger test; bit 5: freed at the path's end), and with the one-shot bit (+3 bit 6) the record keeps no map entry (+$0C/+$0D = 0), so the entry is never re-armed. x = column x 8 (+4), y = (row - $88CF) x 8 (+3).
> Evidence: 1471 runs in 59 builds, from c1 (28) on; the behaviour-$10 branch 722 runs.
> Witness: L1 3254 (long-l4, rzx-l1-00000-poke, rzx-l1-02000-poke, rzx-l1-04000-poke, rzx-l1-06000-poke, rzx-l1-08000-poke, rzx-l1-10000-poke, rzx-l1-12000-poke, rzx-l1-14000-poke, rzx-l1-16000-poke, rzx-l1-18000-poke, rzx-l1-20000-poke, rzx-l1-22000-poke, rzx-l1-24000-poke, rzx-l2-00000-poke, rzx-l2-02000-poke, rzx-l2-04000-poke, rzx-l2-06000-poke, rzx-l2-08000-poke, rzx-l2-10000-poke, rzx-l2-12000-poke, rzx-l2-14000-poke, rzx-l2-16000-poke, rzx-l2-18000-poke, rzx-l2-20000-poke, rzx-l2-22000-poke, rzx-l3-00000-poke, rzx-l3-02000-poke, rzx-l3-04000-poke, rzx-l3-06000-poke, rzx-l3-08000-poke, rzx-l3-10000-poke, rzx-l4-00000-poke, rzx-l4-02000-poke, rzx-l4-04000-poke, rzx-l4-06000-poke, rzx-l4-08000-poke, rzx-l4-10000-poke, rzx-l4-12000-poke, rzx-l4-14000-poke, rzx-l4-16000-poke, rzx-l4-18000-poke, rzx-l5-00000-poke, rzx-l5-02000-poke, rzx-l5-04000-poke, rzx-l5-06000-poke, rzx-l5-08000-poke, rzx-l5-10000-poke, rzx-l5-12000-poke, rzx-l5-14000-poke, rzx-l5-16000-poke, rzx-l5-18000-poke, rzx-l5-20000-poke, rzx-l5-22000-poke, rzx-l5-full, c1, c48, load-l2-load-l5, sec-l2-s7, sec-l2-s10-sec-l2-s12, sec-l3-s5, sec-l3-s7-sec-l3-s9, sec-l4-s x5, sec-l5-s3, sec-l5-s5).
